Overlay patch 0018: name the game entry SDL_main on iOS (2ship trap #2).
Game.cpp defines plain main() on non-Windows; at link it wins over SDL2main's
main(), silently bypassing the UIKit shim: no UIApplicationMain, no UIKit app
context, SDL_CreateWindow returns NULL, boot SIGSEGVs far away. (Upstream's
`extern "C"` under PLATFORM_IOS shows intent, but SDL_main.h's rename macro
does not fire in this TU.) With SDL_main exported, SDL2main's main() runs
UIApplicationMain and calls SDL_main on the main thread after launch.
Desktop unaffected. Caught by build-sim.sh's nm assertion, not at runtime.

--- a/src/port/Game.cpp
+++ b/src/port/Game.cpp
@@ -31,10 +31,13 @@
 
 #ifdef _WIN32
 int SDL_main(int argc, char **argv) {
+#elif defined(PLATFORM_IOS)
+// SOH_IOS (overlay 0018): SDL2main's UIKit shim owns main() on iOS — it runs
+// UIApplicationMain and calls SDL_main on the main thread after launch.
+// Naming this main() wins the link over SDL2main's and bypasses the shim
+// (no UIKit app context; SDL_CreateWindow returns NULL). 2ship trap #2.
+extern "C" int SDL_main(int argc, char* argv[]) {
 #else
-#if defined(__cplusplus) && defined(PLATFORM_IOS)
-extern "C"
-#endif
 int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
 #endif
     GameEngine::Create();
